add_body(doc,'HAKI Version Control is a developer workspace and governance layer designed to organize repositories and connect software changes with validation evidence and human review. It is intended to work alongside Git and GitHub rather than replace them. The project studies a common coordination problem: repository policies, scan results, review decisions, and publication activity can be distributed across tools and may not refer to the same exact revision.')
add_body(doc,'The codebase is a monorepo with a React-based browser client, an Express and TypeScript API, shared validation schemas, PostgreSQL data models through Prisma, and Redis/BullMQ worker processing. The client currently supports a public HAKI page, authentication entry points, a repository dashboard, repository creation/import views, file-tree navigation, code display, settings, and About information. Browser-local storage is used for repository demonstration data. The backend contains authentication and GitHub OAuth modules, token rotation, team/repository/submission/review data models, and an asynchronous validation pipeline using Gitleaks, Semgrep, and Trivy.')
add_body(doc,'The report documents requirements, architecture, data relationships, workflows, security controls, scanner processing, test strategy, interface design, limitations, and future work. The present implementation is a working prototype with meaningful backend foundations, but the client and server are not yet a complete production-integrated workflow. Commit-bound evidence is the principal design principle: validation and approval should refer to the same immutable commit SHA.')
